WEBVTT

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:12.960
Priscilla!

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.570
Thanks, Seira!

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.800
All right, then I'll...

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.470
All right!

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.590
Take this! Make sure you 
go out with a bang.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:57.710
Seira!

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:58.570
Right!

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:07.580
It's a good thing you came, 
Seira. You're a lifesaver.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.940
It's rare for two to attack at once.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.880
Is it true that you asked Etia-san 
yourself if you could help out?

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.180
I want to learn various 
ways of fighting.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.680
So, how'd we do?

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.750
It was very easy fighting with you.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:25.430
Your teamwork was very smooth,

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.060
and you have no hesitation 
in exterminating them.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.070
Well, we've been a 
team for a while now.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.070
Your team may be a 
little insecure still.

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.720
Team...

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.920
I'm... just doing my job.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.080
I've never thought of 
us as a team. Not once.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.590
Well, if you can't figure things 
out, why not talk to Etia-san?

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.310
Does it bother you that 
much that Akari can hear

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.860
the voices of the Daemonia?

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.590
There's no point. It gets in 
the way of fighting, and...

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:05.100
I can't feel sorry for the people 
who were turned into Daemonia.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.190
<b>To the Ends with the Star</b>

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.200
It's nice out today, so 
we're all eating outside.

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:47.950
Come with us, Minori.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.600
Well, I'm...

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.960
Hanae, aren't you coming?

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.210
All the good spots are gonna be taken!

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.210
Sorry, I'm going to pass.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.560
I see.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.220
We'll be on the roof, so if 
you change your mind, come up!

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.720
Minori's a little unusual, isn't she?

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.170
You think so?

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.980
I mean, she's always reading 
books about space.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.960
And she doesn't really try 
to get along with others.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.590
She's sort of dull.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:19.070
But the weirdest thing is that 
you're friends with her, Hanae.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.510
Huh? Why?

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.600
You're like total opposites.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.300
But we've been good friends 
ever since elementary school,

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.330
and we have a lot to talk about.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.940
Minori's really nice, and 
you may say she's dull,

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.350
but I think she's got 
her priorities straight.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.720
Minori! Let's go home!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.080
You don't need to wait 
for the other girls?

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.810
Yeah. It's not like I have to 
go home with them every day.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.310
Wow. These are cute!

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.080
How do I look?

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.400
Yeah, it's cute!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.790
Here, put it on.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:07.800
What? That's okay, 
it's a little too flashy for me.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.490
Really? I think it'd look great on you.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.120
If I had to pick...

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.900
That hair accessory is really cute!

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:23.740
Eh?

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.340
If you're looking for ones with 
stars, there're some over here.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.320
Thank you so much

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.660
for telling us about these 
wonderful hair accessories.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.610
Glad I could help!

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.610
What are you two here to buy?

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.150
Gym equipment.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:44.140
The one that makes your chest 
muscles three times bigger!

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:46.040
Though if you use it 
too much, your boobs

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.740
will turn into muscle, so 
you gotta be careful.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.490
They haven't yet.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.740
You want them to?

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.750
So, you really like stars, Minori?

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:00.490
Yes...

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.710
She's always had a tendency

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.760
to get a little obsessed 
when it comes to stars.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.520
It's good to have something 
that you like.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.250
Huh?

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:21.270
Right? I always think 
that's really great about her,

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.560
especially since I don't have anything.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:28.390
Weird. It sort of looks like 
you two are total opposites,

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:29.530
but you get along?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.480
Yeah, we get told that a lot.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:34.160
I don't know why people 
say that all the time,

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:38.790
but it's totally normal 
for us to be together.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.520
I think I can sort of 
understand that.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:47.280
I'm glad we met the two of you!

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.090
Thank you.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.280
Let's hang out again sometime!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.090
See you later!

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:53.780
That was a lot of fun!

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.100
Yeah, it was.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:58.270
I wonder how long it's been since 
I talked to normal people.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:06:59.810
Yeah...

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:03.450
You're not yourself today, Seira.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:07.760
It's not like you to agree with others,

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.760
especially with someone you just met.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:11.610
That never happens!

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:14.070
Really?

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.420
They were really great.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.080
Yeah, I hope we see them again.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.130
And they gave us their email addresses.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.630
Huh?

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:33.540
I could have sworn I put 
my phone in my bag.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:34.140
What?

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:39.340
98, 99, 100...

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.650
<i>Oh, this is cute!</i>

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.070
<i>What's this animal, Manami?</i>

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.140
<i>What? You don't know, Seira?</i>

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:53.810
<i>It's an alpaca.</i>

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:56.660
<i>It's in the Cetartiodactyla order 
and lives in South Africa.</i>

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:57.660
<i>Ceta...</i>

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:00.660
<i>I don't really get it, 
but you know a lot.</i>

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.070
<i>Every grade schooler knows that!</i>

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:07.440
<i>I want it, but I don't 
have enough pocket money.</i>

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.670
<i>I guess I might have to 
wait until New Year's.</i>

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:33.590
Hello?

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:36.870
<i>Seira? Sorry, it's me, Hanae.</i>

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:39.720
<i>That phone is actually Minori's.</i>

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:40.620
Eh?

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:43.620
I'm so sorry!

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:47.790
I apparently accidentally 
put it in your bag.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.270
It's not a big deal.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:52.800
And we got to see each other again.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.470
Seira-chan...

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.790
We're happy to have 
met you, too, Seira!

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:57.640
Yeah!

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:02.810
But I really am sorry. 
Oh, I'll go buy seconds.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:03.990
You'll both have another, right?

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:06.110
Don't worry about it, Minori. I'll get...

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.100
It's oka—

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.320
Minori?! Minori!

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.330
Someone call an ambulance! Please!

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:29.590
Minori's had heart problems 
ever since she was born.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.170
They actually have to operate 
on her as soon as possible.

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.790
But they haven't been able to and 
they've been waiting for years.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.600
Apparently it's a rather 
difficult surgery.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:43.160
She's been fainting quite a bit lately.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.900
Each time, Minori says she's 
fine and laughs it off,

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.350
even though she must 
be scared to death.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.360
Minori's helped me out so many times.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:57.520
My parents didn't get along,

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:00.630
and I just got sick of everything.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:04.290
I didn't know how to get 
along with anyone in class,

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:07.870
but Minori was the only 
one who talked to me.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.840
That's why I...

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:15.380
Is there something I can do?

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:19.340
Is there something I can do for Minori?

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:24.250
Just do what you can.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.100
What you think that you can do.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.090
Yeah, you're right.

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:44.620
<i>Can I get this, please?</i>

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.250
<i>Is it a gift?</i>

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:50.620
<i>Yes! It's for a birthday!</i>

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:00.130
<i>I wonder if Manami will be happy. </i>{alt: I wonder if Manami will like it.}

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.460
<i>What is that?</i>

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:15.460
<i>Is that the Daemonia my 
mom was talking about?!</i>

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:22.280
<i>Manami!</i>

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.800
<i>Manami! Manami?!</i>

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:35.380
<i>Manami!</i>

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:36.440
<i>Seira!</i>

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:37.550
<i>Are you okay?!</i>

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:41.130
<i>Yeah, but what's with this wind?</i>

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.380
<i>It's really creepy.</i>

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:48.150
<i>I'm the only one that can see it.</i>

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:51.800
<i>At this rate, everyone is...</i>

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.640
<i>But how am I supposed to fight it?</i>

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:11.920
<i>Seira!</i>

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:16.420
<i>Manami!</i>

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.480
<i>Manami...</i>

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:42.480
<i>The only thing I can do right now</i>

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:46.020
<i>is to exterminate the Daemonia.</i>

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:54.290
I'm really sorry for making you worry.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:58.030
They think I can be discharged 
in two or three days.

00:12:58.030 --> 00:12:59.250
I see...

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:04.010
I'm so sorry. I always 
cause you so much trouble.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:08.010
And I tell you every time that you 
don't have to worry about it.

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:13.520
Really, thank you so much.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.660
Have you thought about it?

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.720
You want to help her, right?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.780
I don't think she has much time left.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.790
The choice

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:36.980
is yours.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.580
<i>Just do what you can.</i>

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:54.630
What's that?

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:57.320
Oh, I'm writing down 
everything that the people

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:59.220
I've heard have said so I don't forget.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.880
I thought that maybe if I wrote it down,

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.040
I might be able to understand—

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:05.770
Understand?

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:09.660
There's nothing to understand. 
It's pointless.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:12.980
You can't tell if you 
haven't heard the voices.

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:17.860
It does make exterminating a bit 
harder, but we can help with that.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:18.670
Ginka...

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:21.970
"We can help with that"? 
For the Daemonia?

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:22.920
You've got to be kidding.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.290
Seira...

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:26.920
Leave her be. She doesn't get it.

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.530
You want to leave your team?

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:34.990
Why is that?

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.830
As long as Akari can hear 
the Daemonia's voices,

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:39.560
I can't fight with her.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.940
I'd like to join Meltina-san's 
team if possible.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.920
Well, I guess it 
wouldn't be a bad idea

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:47.430
to split the teams three and three.

00:14:49.210 --> 00:14:50.360
Just once more...

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:55.960
Why not fight with them just once more?

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.120
And if you don't feel any 
differently after that...

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.450
All right.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.630
Do you have some plan?

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:14.760
I do. Right now, Seira 
needs them, that team.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.710
Um, uh...

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:26.610
It's not that I don't like you.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:30.650
I just don't want to 
do pointless things.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.850
I think there is a point, though.

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:37.160
I think this is what I'm meant to do.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.160
We won't be able to get along.

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:41.920
Why?

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.320
Because that's who I am.

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:54.600
Hello?

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.930
Oh, Seira-chan? Have 
you heard from Hanae?

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:01.680
I haven't been able to get a hold of 
her since the day before yesterday.

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:05.330
She said she'd come visit 
me again yesterday, too.

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:33.590
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.350
<i>It can't be... It can't be!</i>

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:47.900
Seira-san?

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:51.650
This isn't good!

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:56.410
What's wrong with you, Seira?!

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:03.910
She's your friend, right, Seira?

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:07.990
She's calling out your 
name right now.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.770
She says she wants to talk to you.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:13.760
But...

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:16.770
If you don't talk to her 
right now, you'll regret it.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:36.580
So it was you, Seira.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:37.520
Why?

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:41.990
Because I don't have the money 
to pay for Minori's surgery,

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:44.500
and I had nothing else 
that I could give her.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.000
But, this?!

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:49.720
Selling my soul to a demon...

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:52.500
I shouldn't have done that, huh?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.130
I'm sorry, I...

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:00.080
My body won't listen to me.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:04.520
At this rate, I might 
kill someone else.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:05.520
Hanae...

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:08.520
My heart hurts...

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.030
That's...

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:19.430
Please take care of Minori.

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:33.960
Seira! Finish it!

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:46.480
I can't...

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:47.810
What the hell are you doing?!

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:53.940
Seira-san!

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.860
We have to take responsibility 
for hearing their voices.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:02.490
Not being able to exterminate it 
just because you heard its voice

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:04.570
just means you lack resolve!

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:05.490
Akari...

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:09.360
We heard her voice. And 
that's exactly why...

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:18.050
Seira!

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:26.230
<i>What I can do for my friends...</i>

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.970
But I'm really happy for Minori-chan

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:47.010
that she found a donor so suddenly.

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:50.820
Yes, we hadn't been able to 
find one all of these years.

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:53.580
Though I do feel bad for 
the person that passed.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:56.250
Now as long as the 
surgery is a success...

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:03.590
Oh, Seira-chan...

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:06.900
How do you feel? I heard you're 
going to have that surgery.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.350
Yes, tomorrow.

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:13.710
I sort of feel like god 
arranged this surgery for me.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:19.860
Huh? The same one as mine?

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:23.860
I want you to keep it 
since it was Hanae's.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.210
Hanae?

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.790
I don't really understand, 
but thank you.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.380
May I sit next to you?

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:48.620
Sure.

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:56.670
My cousin became a Daemonia.

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:57.510
Huh?

00:20:57.510 --> 00:20:59.240
I don't know why,

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:01.730
and I won't be able to find out anymore.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:06.740
In the end, I...

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:11.650
I'm sure you have 
your own ideas, Seira.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:16.490
But for me, hearing their 
voices is very important.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:22.760
I had no other choice 
but to hate them.

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:25.510
I kept exterminating and exterminating,

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:28.070
and tried not to think 
too much about it.

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:30.060
As long as I thought it was 
their fault for becoming

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:31.900
a Daemonia, it made things easier.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.080
I wanted to avenge my friend.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:37.850
That was how I felt 
every time I fought.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:40.770
Even though that won't 
bring Manami back.

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:45.280
But I couldn't hate Hanae.

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:48.100
I still hate the Daemonia.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:49.730
Hanae and Manami...

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:51.710
They keep robbing me of 
those precious to me.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:56.290
The one that lacked resolve was me.

00:21:57.570 --> 00:21:58.620
I was scared

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:01.860
that something inside me would break.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:07.050
I felt that if I heard their voices, 
I'd be betraying Manami.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:29.880
<b>The Empress means fruitful situations, 
and gentle motherly love.</b>

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:42.400
<b>#03  The Empress</b>

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:30.050
It's us, Lapschrö, meow. This 
week's card is The Empress.

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:33.340
<b>It is a good card, and if you value little 
pleasures and feeling fulfilled, you'll be 
able to feel the same kind of gentleness 
and kindness as a mother would give.</b>

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:32.040
I guess I wouldn't mind 
explaining this week's card.

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:33.500
Wow, so you actually feel 
like doing your job, meow.

00:23:33.340 --> 00:23:37.810
<b>If you were to choose this card, it shows
 that you have a very big, kind heart, and 
look at the outcome of situations from a
 broad point of view. You should be able 
to obtain present riches by believing 
in the future.</b>

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:34.830
By the way, The Empress 
means femininity,

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:37.190
wealth, growth, to nurture...

00:23:37.190 --> 00:23:39.530
Wha— I don't have any reason 
to explain it anymore!

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:42.400
<b>However, if the card is reversed, 
you will concentrate only on your 
own thoughts and feelings, making 
you self-centered and selfish, and 
lose your chance because you 
became unaware of your surroundings.</b>

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:41.390
<b>A Lovely Holiday</b>

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:41.830
See you next time!
